 reference only.\nUse it to preserve the football pitch, green grass, white field lines, goal, blue spectator stands, dense penguin audience, GUGA FC / DORO FC team-color atmosphere, and the overall cute polished 3D stadium world throughout the full video.\n\nAll reference pictures are visual references rather than mandatory keyframes, except that the video should begin close to the situation shown in <Picture 4>.\n\nDo NOT construct the video as interpolation between reference pictures.\nDo NOT try to recreate later timestamps by forcing the video to match any reference image exactly.\nGenerate the middle and ending parts naturally according to the described story and physical actions.\n\n\nTARGET VIDEO\n\nCreate one continuous cute but dramatic chibi football sequence in a packed mini football stadium.\n\nThe story progression is:\n\nThe Penguin Player (S1) is dribbling the football forward.\nThe Pink-haired Player (S2) quickly closes in to challenge.\nAfter a short chase and pressure, S2 performs a committed slide tackle.\nThe tackle knocks the ball loose and also knocks S1 off balance.\nS1 tumbles onto the grass in a cute but physically believable way.\nThe football rolls away across the field.\nThe crowd reacts.\nA sharp referee whistle is heard.\nThe Blonde Referee (S3) runs into the scene.\nS3 approaches S2, firmly raises a yellow card, and gives one brief verbal decision.\nAfter the referee's decision, the remaining action consists of silent visual reactions from the players and referee.\n\nThe entire sequence must feel like one natural continuous football moment, not a slideshow or image morph.\n\nOPENING\n\nBegin close to the football-match setup shown in <Picture 4>.\n\nUse a lively medium-wide football-broadcast feeling.\nS1 is controlling the ball near the attacking area.\nS2 is approaching from the front-right side and preparing to defend.\nOther players may move naturally in the background, but S1 and S2 remain the main focus.\nThe penguin audience in the stadium reacts energetically.\nThe camera may gently track the action forward while keeping the ball visible.\n\nACTION DEVELOPMENT\n\nS1 continues dribbling with short quick chibi football steps.\nS2 closes the distance, pressures S1, and then commits to a sliding tackle.\n\nThe tackle must be shown as a real continuous physical motion, not as a dissolve or abrupt jump.\n\nS2's sliding leg reaches the ball, the ball is knocked loose, and S1 loses balance.\nS1 spreads her flipper-like arms instinctively and tumbles onto the grass in a cute but dramatic way.\n\nAt the moment of losing balance, S1 gives one brief cry: <d>[Chinese] 哎呀！</d>\n\nS2 continues sliding briefly because of momentum.\n\nThe football rolls several feet away.\nNearby players react with surprise.\nThe crowd gives a shocked reaction.\n\nKeep character anatomy, costume design, hairstyles, and proportions stable during fast action.\n\nREFEREE MOMENT\n\nImmediately after the foul, a loud referee whistle is heard.\n\nS1 is sitting or kneeling on the grass, looking surprised, hurt, and slightly aggrieved.\nS2 starts getting up and looks surprised, then slightly nervous or guilty.\n\nS3, the Blonde Referee, runs into the scene wearing the black referee uniform defined by <Picture 3>.\nS3 must remain visually consistent with <Picture 3> and must clearly remain the referee.\n\nS3 approaches S2, stops in front of her, firmly raises one clearly visible yellow card toward the pink-haired player, and delivers one single short decision:\n\n<d>[Chinese] 犯规，黄牌！</d>\n\nImmediately after completing this single utterance, S3 closes her mouth and remains silent while continuing to hold the yellow card toward S2.\n\nENDING\n\nFor the remainder of the video, continue with visual reactions only.\n\nS3 remains silent, keeps her attention on S2, and holds the yellow card visibly for a moment before naturally relaxing her arm slightly.\n\nS2 understands the decision. Her expression shifts from surprise to embarrassment and disappointment. She slightly lowers her head, averts her eyes for a moment, and looks frustrated.\n\nS1 remains sitting or kneeling on the grass and watches the referee and S2 with a mildly aggrieved expression.\n\nNearby players slow down and gather naturally. Some look toward S2, while others look toward the referee or S1.\n\nThe football remains away from the main group after the tackle.\n\nThe stadium crowd continues reacting in the background.\n\nAll characters remain silent during this final reaction phase. Their mouths stay naturally closed except for non-verbal facial reactions.\n\nLet the motion progressively settle into a clear football-match tableau: the referee facing the offending player with the yellow card visible, S2 looking embarrassed, and S1 watching from the grass.\n\nHold this natural reaction composition through the end of the generated clip.\n\nAUDIO\n\nDialogue and vocal reactions occur only at the exact moments embedded in the action description above.\n\nAfter the referee finishes her single yellow-card decision, the remainder of the clip contains no spoken dialogue. Continue with stadium ambience and physical sound only.\n\nOverall soundscape:\nenergetic football stadium ambience, penguin crowd cheering and reacting, running footsteps on grass, football contact sounds, soft sliding grass friction, a cute but impactful foul collision, one clear referee whistle associated with the foul, and sustained crowd reaction during the yellow-card aftermath.\n\nMusic:\ncute energetic sports music during the football action,\na brief dramatic-comedic accent during the tackle,\nthen lighter tension during the referee and yellow-card moment,\nsettling gently underneath the final silent reactions.\n\nCONSISTENCY PRIORITIES\n\n<Picture 1> strongly controls the Penguin Player identity.\n<Picture 2> strongly controls the Pink-haired Player identity.\n<Picture 3> strongly controls the Blonde Referee identity and referee outfit.\n<Picture 4> strongly controls the opening match setup and initial football composition.\n<Picture 5> strongly controls the stadium world, football field environment, and overall visual style.\n\nDo not merge the three main character identities.\nDo not exchange their uniforms or hairstyles.\nDo not change the referee into a football player.\nDo not overpopulate the foreground with duplicate main characters.\nKeep the entire video in the same polished cute chibi 3D toy-like football aesthetic.\n"], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "value"}], "flags": {}, "type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline", "title": "Input Text (Prompt)", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#533", "size": [370, 390], "pos": [-1480, 6000], "id": 138, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"}, "order": 13}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#222", "widgets_values": ["# MiniMax H3 咕嘎FC｜简要说明\n\n## 1. 参考图分工\n\n* **Picture 1**：企鹅球员角色参考\n* **Picture 2**：粉色丸子头球员角色参考\n* **Picture 3**：黄发裁判角色与服装参考\n* **Picture 4**：视频开始状态参考\n* **Picture 5**：球场环境与整体风格参考\n\n## 2. 图片对应关系\n\n工作流按连接顺序对应：\n\n* `ref_image_0` → `<Picture 1>`\n* `ref_image_1` → `<Picture 2>`\n* `ref_image_2` → `<Picture 3>`\n* `ref_image_3` → `<Picture 4>`\n* `ref_image_4` → `<Picture 5>`\n\n更换图片或顺序时，Prompt 中的 Picture 编号也要同步调整。\n\n## 3. Prompt 写法\n\n提示词主要写三部分：\n\n* **角色定义**：每个 Picture 对应谁、需要保持哪些外观特征\n* **动作流程**：按顺序描述“谁做什么 → 接下来发生什么 → 结果是什么”\n* **结尾状态**：对白结束后，用表情、站位和环境反应完成收尾\n\n动作建议写完整过程，例如：\n\n**带球 → 逼抢 → 滑铲 → 球滚开 → 摔倒 → 裁判进场 → 黄牌 → 无对白反应收尾**\n\n## 4. 当前模板\n\n* S1：企鹅球员\n* S2：粉色丸子头球员\n* S3：黄发裁判\n* 时长：12 秒\n* 比例：16:9\n* 核心节点：`MiniMaxH3ReferenceToVideo` \n\n"], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "MarkdownNote", "title": "Note: MiniMax H3", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#000", "size": [445.4465637207031, 704.5149536132812], "pos": [-2030, 4850], "id": 116, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}}, "order": 14}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#222", "widgets_values": ["0.7,13秒的视频,Urlta